inst/autogenerate_plots/generated
inst/autogenerate_plots/params_log.txt
# tools/render_vignettes.R writes doc/*.md and doc/*_files/ -- those
# are deliberately tracked (so GitHub can render them with figures);
# the throwaway HTML/R/Rmd copies devtools::build_vignettes() also
# drops in doc/ are not. Scoped to these three extensions specifically,
# not a blanket doc/ ignore, so a genuinely new tracked file under
# doc/ (a new vignette's .md, its own _files/) still shows up as
# untracked instead of silently needing `git add -f` to even be
# noticed -- a blanket doc/ ignore (this repo's own past setup, in the
# untracked .git/info/exclude rather than here) is exactly how three
# doc/boxplots_files/figure-gfm/box-extended*.png files ended up
# committed nowhere despite doc/boxplots.md already linking to them.
doc/*.html
doc/*.R
doc/*.Rmd
Meta/
# reference material: the internal originals stay untracked; only the
# anonymised plot snippets and the (already published) reference PNGs are
# committed. reference_code.txt and the nicerplot/ clone remain ignored.
references/*
!references/README.md
!references/plots/
!references/code/
references/code/*
!references/code/reference_plot_snippets.R
ggcpb.Rproj
